					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=388108&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973922" alt="Djoric" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=388108)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/djoric" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(388108); return false;" >Djoric</a></span> <span class="odate time_1388192654 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Dec 2013 01:04</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1923633">
									

<p>The Esoteric Warfare Unit is the Foundation's answer to getting repeatedly curbstomped by everyone else out there who's fielding augmented agents. It's a small, underfunded collection of mages, psychics, cyborgs, and other assorted oddities, scraped together and put into a . Of course, it is existing in the shadow of the disaster of Omega-7 back in the 90s, and so makes sure to put everything through rigorous testing, generally getting their equipment through the Site 87 labs rather than Dr. Foster's R&amp;D department. The individuals in the program are a wide array of people, brought in from both outside and inside the Foundation.</p>
<p>Think less X-men, and more BRPD.</p>
<p>As far as the erotic carrot hivemind goes, it is a hallucination brought on by a combination of sleep deprivation and psychic sensitivity, being that of a bundle of carrots sharing the same consciousness and being very naughty.</p>

